<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gaza (312 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">312 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-diadochi">Wars of the Diadochi</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gaza was fought in 312 BCE between Demetrius, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> I, and the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus</a>. Ptolemy and Seleucus won. Seleucus was then able to return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and recover his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a>, an event traditionally taken as the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p></div>
